<header class="page-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">Privacy information</p><h1>How FurniCraft handles your information.</h1><p>This notice describes the privacy controls implemented in this FurniCraft prototype. It is not a claim of formal legal compliance.</p></div></header>
<article class="panel vstack gap-3">
    <section><h2 class="h5">Room photos and AI consent</h2><p>Room photos are stored in private application storage and served only to the signed-in owner and authorized shop administrators. New uploads have EXIF and common image text metadata removed before storage. The AI checkbox is optional. If you leave it unchecked, FurniCraft uses local planning guidance and does not send that photo to Gemini. If you opt in, the photo may be sent to Google Gemini through the configured API for room analysis and a generated furnished preview. You can turn off future AI processing for an image or delete it; this cannot recall data already sent to the provider. Photos uploaded before this consent control was introduced are not retroactively treated as consented, and any prior provider processing cannot be undone by this setting.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="h5">Other account information</h2><p>FurniCraft stores account and contact details, preferences, recommendation history, catalog interactions, and reservation requests to provide the service. Reservation and recommendation history is removed with your account through the self-service account deletion control. Operational privacy audit entries record consent, image transfer, deletion, and retention actions without storing the photo contents or your network address.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="h5">Retention and deletion</h2><p>Room photos and generated previews are scheduled for deletion after {{ (int) config('privacy.room_image_retention_days', 90) }} days. You can delete an image sooner from your room list. Account deletion removes the associated account data. An administrator may configure the room-photo retention period using <code>ROOM_IMAGE_RETENTION_DAYS</code>.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="h5">External processing</h2><p>When you consent, room photos are transmitted to Google Gemini for the purposes shown beside the consent control. The shop operator configures the API account and should review the provider’s current terms and data handling information before production use. Do not upload photos containing people, identity documents, or other sensitive information.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="h5">Questions or requests</h2><p>Use <a href="{{ auth()->check() && !auth()->user()->isAdmin() ? route('profile.edit') : route('home') }}">profile settings</a> to delete your account, or contact Lance Furniture Shop staff for help with a data request.</p></section>
